A||||5||CUTTER||Drop Motor For Exhaust Manifold?||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||07-01-2000||12:42 AM||||I have a exhaust leak in my back manifold. Would I be able to take off the rear deck too get to it or drop the motor? Im thinking of telling my garage when they have it off to give it too me to grind down the restrictions if they wont do it. Mainly because i dont have the tools. What should I do?<BR>Thanks, Shane<BR>87GT<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Oreif||07-01-2000||01:37 AM||||I was able to remove both of my Exhaust manifolds and install my Sprint manifolds without dropping the engine nor removing the decklid. The top bolts you can get to from the top and the bottom ones from the bottom. The real hard one is the one between the A/C compressor and the coolant tube. I used a small wrench and lots of muscle.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||07-01-2000||02:18 AM||||Yep, What he said...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||07-01-2000||02:53 AM||||Im in the process of replacing my exhaust manifold (the forward one, the one by the back glass). Its a SERIOUS pain in the a%#! However, I did remove the decklid (87 GT) to help, and it does. Not only that, but the decklid removal is extremely simple. Just take off the 4 bolts, thats it! (You may also want to mark them before removing)<BR>Ive still got 2 bolts left on the manifold...lower center and lower right hand side...you know, the "hard ones".....eeek!<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 07-01-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||07-01-2000||05:05 AM||||Did any of the bolts snap off on you guys when removing? When Tom sends me the set from my parts car this month after porting/welding I'm thinking of attempting myself, but my BIGGEST nightmare is hearing "snap". Couldn't imagine trying to extract a bolt without dropping the engine then if it was the one by the glass.<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||5
Z||000005||Taijiguy||07-01-2000||05:58 AM||||That's always a possibility..happened on two of mine. I suppose the one redeeming factor is that I did already have the motor out. In fact, on of the stud towers cracked, so I have a bit of welding to do. Hope that doesn't happen to you......<P><BR>Taiji<BR>modified 85 GT||||reg||1
